{% include "ent-connections.njk" %}

      {#- Why we build it (founder, 2026-11-16): on the home page 2026-11-17,
          on About 2026-11-19, back on the home page 2026-11-21 (founder),
          after the bots and before Connections; below Connections
          since later that day (founder), with its copy cut to a few
          sentences. Greiner's phases of growth (HBR), redrawn from his
          consulting work with no client named, with two ways in: early, at
          the crisis of leadership, and later, after the crisis of autonomy.
          It draws itself when it scrolls into view (/enterprise/charts.js);
          without it, or with Reduce Motion, it stays still and complete. -#}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="why-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="why-h">Why we build it</h2>
        <h3 class="ent-h">Every startup reaches the same scaling points. We build for them.</h3>
        <div class="ent-charts ent-charts--one">
          <figure class="ent-chart">
            <figcaption class="ent-chart-title">The scaling points are predictable <button class="ent-replay" type="button" hidden aria-label="Replay the chart">Replay</button></figcaption>
            <div class="ent-chart-frame">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 640 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="c1-t c1-d" data-stops="254:1700:1100,462:1500:700,520:600:1100,612:1100:0">
                <title id="c1-t">Phases of growth, and two ways in</title>
                <desc id="c1-d">A company grows through three phases, creativity, direction and delegation. The usual path dips at a crisis of leadership between the first two, and at a crisis of autonomy between the last two it turns downward and keeps sliding. Two OpenShore paths leave it. Coming in early, at the first crisis, the line climbs straight through both crises: delegation built in. Coming in later, after the second crisis has started the slide, the line bends back upward: course corrected.</desc>
                <line class="c-axis" x1="30" y1="274" x2="500" y2="274" />
                <g class="c-legend">
                  <line class="c-key c-key--sea" x1="44" y1="29" x2="64" y2="29" />
                  <text x="72" y="34">With OpenShore</text>
                  <line class="c-key c-key--risk" x1="196" y1="29" x2="216" y2="29" />
                  <text x="224" y="34">The usual path</text>
                </g>
                <g class="c-plot" transform="matrix(0.785 0 0 1 9.46 0)">
                  <line class="c-guide c-rv" data-x="250" x1="262" y1="80" x2="262" y2="272" />
                  <line class="c-guide c-rv" data-x="450" x1="456" y1="80" x2="456" y2="272" />
                  <path class="c-line c-line--risk c-draw" d="M44 256 Q170 244 254 194 L270 222 Q360 206 446 150 L462 178 Q540 204 612 236" />
                  <path class="c-line c-line--sea c-draw" d="M254 194 Q420 150 612 58" />
                  <path class="c-line c-line--sea c-line--late c-draw" d="M520 198.5 C552 196 580 132 612 104" />
                </g>
                <text class="c-crisis c-rv c-pop" data-x="252" x="224.6" y="124" text-anchor="middle">crisis of leadership</text>
                <text class="c-crisis c-rv c-pop" data-x="450" x="367.4" y="68" text-anchor="middle">crisis of autonomy</text>
                <line class="c-leader c-rv c-late" data-x="252" x1="154" y1="176" x2="197.9" y2="190" />
                <text class="c-mark c-rv c-pop c-late" data-x="252" x="150" y="172" text-anchor="end">Come in early</text>
                <circle class="c-ripple" data-x="252" cx="208.9" cy="194" r="13" />
                <circle class="c-halo c-rv" data-x="252" cx="208.9" cy="194" r="13" />
                <circle class="c-dot c-rv" data-x="252" cx="208.9" cy="194" r="6" />
                <line class="c-leader c-rv c-late" data-x="516" x1="397.7" y1="214" x2="408.7" y2="205" />
                <text class="c-mark c-rv c-pop c-late" data-x="516" x="393.7" y="228" text-anchor="end">Or come in later</text>
                <circle class="c-ripple" data-x="516" cx="417.7" cy="198.5" r="13" />
                <circle class="c-halo c-rv" data-x="516" cx="417.7" cy="198.5" r="13" />
                <circle class="c-dot c-rv" data-x="516" cx="417.7" cy="198.5" r="6" />
                <text class="c-end c-end--sea c-rv c-pop" data-x="600" x="504" y="63">Built in early</text>
                <text class="c-end c-end--wave c-rv c-pop" data-x="600" x="504" y="109">Course corrected</text>
                <text class="c-end c-end--risk c-rv c-pop" data-x="600" x="504" y="241">Keeps sliding</text>
                <text class="c-phase c-dim" data-x="44" x="127.2" y="302" text-anchor="middle">CREATIVITY</text>
                <text class="c-phase c-dim" data-x="262" x="291.3" y="302" text-anchor="middle">DIRECTION</text>
                <text class="c-phase c-dim" data-x="456" x="433.4" y="302" text-anchor="middle">DELEGATION</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="ent-body">Growth comes in phases, and each one ends in a crisis. First the founders become the bottleneck. Then teams need to decide on their own, with no shared standards to decide by, and growth slides. OpenShore puts that direction layer in, early or late, so leaders spend their time on customers, not fire drills.</p>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="ent-source">Source: Larry E. Greiner, “Evolution and Revolution as Organizations Grow,” <i>Harvard Business Review</i> (1972, reissued 1998). The OpenShore paths show where we come in.</p>
      </section>

